To celebrate my parents' birthday, I booked this room myself.

I think the hardware is still beyond expectations:
Although it is a single room, the view is very good, the layout is very transparent, and the 270-degree window is a plus. Even though the bathroom is arranged behind the back, the bathtub is still a landscape bathtub, and the mirror greatly makes the originally closed bathroom become very spacious. transparent;

The service is basically up to standard. Although the Grand Hyatt hotel has an overwhelming number of guests, it can still maintain a certain standard.
Of course, except for the middle-aged greasy male waiter who bullied the young female waiter that I criticized in another comment;

I think the problem of the overall facilities and decoration being old is a matter of time, not the hotel itself. The maintenance is pretty good.
